      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a95256f54d514123c1f089d|full_name}: With SteamVR you can put a custom binding on a controller button but there is no button or button combination in VRChat that is not already in use or that would be pressed accidentally by doing gestures.\nso i would prefer a menu button and it doesn't need to be mute specific one. a custom key bind button would probably have a lot of use cases, like for youtuber or streamer to start and stop a recording.\nso the possibility to add more than one custom button would be even better.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-07-24T04:28:57.556Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be very useful if we could have a second mute button to trigger the custom mute/unmute key bind of our voice chat programs like Discord or TeamSpeak.\nChanging to the desktop view to mute yourself in discord when you are speaking with someone in VR, is really annoying, immersion breaking and too time consuming when someone in VRChat is waiting for your reaction but you want to be muted in voice chat first.\nWith the possibility to tell VRChat the mute/unmute key bind for our favorite voice chat programm and then using it with a simple button click on the menu, we could always quickly mute ourself in the voice chat without interrupting conversations or immersion.",
